Chapter: DeskParseTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFont

 Pins GopDesk's pure pieces: BCD decode of CMOS RTC registers, two-digit
 zero padding, and the window geometry at the 1280x800 scale-2 shape the
 OVMF bed presents.

 These lines used to pin a close-box hit test. Change 12350 removed the
 close box: the "x" glyph and desk-close-hit went together, because the
 desktop is the last screen on the machine and Shutdown is the way out.
 What replaces it is the invariant whose absence was the actual defect --
 the window is sized from its own wrapped text, so the last line lands
 inside the panel with exactly the footer reserve to spare, at every
 scale and under either font. A fixed height is what put the hint line
 26 pixels below the frame.

Section: Fixture

 A LOADED FACE, WITH THE METRICS A LOADED FACE HAS. This stood at
 `gf-ok = True` with every metric ZERO, which is a shape `gfont-load` never
 produces: a face that rasterized has a glyph height. It read as harmless for
 as long as nothing consumed the metrics, and stopped being harmless the day
 `dk-line-step` learned to read the face instead of answering a flat constant.

 The arithmetic, measured 2026-08-25: `dk-line-step` answers `gf-gh * 5 / 4`
 when the face is ok, so a zero height gave a zero line step, `dk-win-h`
 collapsed from 326 to 74, and `dp-slack` went to MINUS 222 -- the wizard's
 text running 222 pixels past a window sized for none of it. The file went red
 at head and stayed red, because nothing in any lane's gate runs it (L-NOGATE);
 the release battery is what would have found it.

 The numbers are CMUNSS at ppem 16, which is what `dk-ui-ppem` asks for at 1600
 and above and what `desk-leading-metrics` prints: a 21 row cell with 11 pixel
 capitals. This is L-CONSTRUCT one level up -- the fixture was built in a shape
 no real input has, so no amount of running it could say so.

 THE `win` ROW MOVED FOR A DIFFERENT AND EQUALLY INTENDED REASON, and it is
 written down here so the next reader does not have to re-derive it.
 `dk-win-x 1280 2` answers 360 where this file recorded 440, because
 `ui-wscale` steps at 1600 and used to step at 1024 (WORKS-35): at 1280 the
 sidebar is 160 device pixels now and was 320 then, and `dk-win-x` is measured
 from the sidebar's right edge. Nothing about the window changed.

 So all four deltas from the recorded expectation have named causes -- the
 face-aware step, this fixture, the realigned walk below, and `ui-wscale` --
 and none of them is a defect in the wizard. Re-recording is correct HERE and
 was not correct before they were each accounted for, which is the whole
 difference between re-baselining and repairing.

  dp-ttf : GopFont
  dp-ttf = GopFont { gf-ok = True, gf-base = 0, gf-gw = 8, gf-gh = 21, gf-asc = 16, gf-cap = 11 }

 THE LEADING IS `dk-line-step`, NOT `dk-line-h`, and this walk is a SHADOW of
 the painter's own. `dk-wizard-draw` steps each paragraph by `dk-line-step tf s`
 and gaps by `dk-para-gap * s`; this re-implemented that with the flat
 `dk-line-h` and an unscaled gap, which was the same arithmetic until
 `dk-line-step` learned to read the face. The painter moved and the shadow did
 not, so the test began comparing a window sized one way against text laid out
 another (L-INSTRUMENT). With a real face that disagreement is 40 pixels; with
 the zero-metric fixture it read as 222 and looked like nonsense.

 It divides by `s` because it is answering in LOGICAL units, which is what
 `dk-win-h` answers in and therefore what `dp-slack` can subtract. The painter
 keeps everything in device pixels and never needs the division.

 So the invariant is now exact rather than approximate: every line the painter
 draws is counted with the step the painter uses, so the slack IS
 `dk-win-pad-b`, at every scale and under either font. A slack that is not the
 footer reserve is the defect, and the number to compare it against is a
 constant rather than a recorded value.

  dp-text-bottom : GopFont, Integer -> Integer
  dp-text-bottom (tf) (s) =
    let cols = dk-wrap-cols s
    in let step = dk-line-step tf s / s
    in let y2 = dk-body-y0 + dk-wrap-count dk-para-intro cols * step + dk-para-gap
    in let y3 = y2 + dk-wrap-count (dk-para-font tf) cols * step + dk-para-gap
    in y3 + dk-wrap-count dk-para-hint cols * step

  dp-slack : GopFont, Integer -> Integer
  dp-slack (tf) (s) = dk-win-h tf s - dp-text-bottom tf s

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("bcd: " & show (dk-bcd 0) & " " & show (dk-bcd 22) & " " & show (dk-bcd 89) & " " & show (dk-bcd 149))
    print-line-uni ("pad2: " & dk-pad2 0 & " " & dk-pad2 9 & " " & dk-pad2 10 & " " & dk-pad2 59)
    print-line-uni ("cols: " & show (dk-wrap-cols 1) & " " & show (dk-wrap-cols 2))
    print-line-uni ("wrap: " & show (dk-wrap-count dk-para-intro 42) & " " & show (dk-wrap-count dk-para-hint 42) & " " & show (dk-wrap-count (dk-para-font gfont-none) 42) & " " & show (dk-wrap-count (dk-para-font dp-ttf) 42))
    print-line-uni ("lines: " & show (dk-body-lines gfont-none 2) & " " & show (dk-body-lines dp-ttf 2))
    print-line-uni ("winh: " & show (dk-win-h gfont-none 2) & " " & show (dk-win-h dp-ttf 2))
    print-line-uni ("slack: " & show (dp-slack gfont-none 1) & " " & show (dp-slack gfont-none 2) & " " & show (dp-slack dp-ttf 2))
    print-line-uni ("win: " & show (dk-win-x 1280 2) & " " & show (dk-win-y 800 2 gfont-none) & " " & show (dk-win-y 800 2 dp-ttf))
  end
